0..65 Comment "/// This source maps loop words to presented and native integers."
66..69 Comment "///"
70..127 Comment "/// The presented fold respects word rules by conversion."
128..182 Comment "/// The native fold uses the native model obligations."
183..261 Comment "/// At `Loop(Unloop(x))` the native fold gives `turn(unturn(native_wind(x)))`,"
262..322 Comment "/// and conversion does not reduce that term for a variable."
323..403 Comment "/// So `respects` names the law `turnUnturn` for the first rule and `unturnTurn`"
404..423 Comment "/// for the second."
424..500 Comment "/// The loop arms call the model\'s operations, so each side of a rule is the"
501..523 Comment "/// endpoint of a law."
524..527 Comment "///"
528..564 Comment "/// The folds map closed loop words."
565..624 Comment "/// The checker reads each fold through its selected model."
625..628 Comment "///"
629..678 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/loop-shape.gandr"
680..706 Comment "// The presented integers."
